  "instruction": "Please list all the people who were added to the FBI's Most Wanted list in 2000 or 2001 who were convicted of murder within the ten years after their placement on the list.",
  "answer": "Based on my research of all 10 individuals added to the FBI's Ten Most Wanted Fugitives list in 2000 and 2001, **five** were convicted of murder within 10 years of their placement:\n\n## Individuals Meeting the Criteria\n\n| Name | FBI # | Date Added | Murder Conviction Date | Within 10 Years |\n|------|-------|------------|------------------------|-----------------|\n| **Jesse James Caston** | 459 | Aug 19, 2000 | Aug 16, 2004 (second-degree murder, Crosby plea) | ✅ Yes |\n| **Aurlieas Dame McClarty** | 461 | Feb 24, 2001 | May 7, 2008 (two counts first-degree murder) | ✅ Yes |\n| **Francis William Murphy** | 464 | Jun 6, 2001 | Aug 4, 2003 (five counts second-degree murder) | ✅ Yes |\n| **Dwight Bowen** | 465 | Aug 30, 2001 | Feb 19, 2004 (two counts second-degree murder) | ✅ Yes |\n| **Felix Summers** | 468 | Oct 30, 2001 | Nov 13, 2006 (first-degree murder) | ✅ Yes |\n\n## Individuals Added in 2000–2001 Who Did NOT Meet Criteria\n\n| Name | FBI # | Date Added | Reason |\n|------|-------|------------|--------|\n| Eric Franklin Rosser | 460 | Dec 27, 2000 | Convicted of child pornography, not murder |\n| Hopeton Eric Brown | 462 | Mar 17, 2001 | Killed in gunfight with Jamaican police (2004); no trial/conviction |\n| Maghfoor Mansoor | 463 | May 23, 2001 | Killed by police in hotel lobby (2001); no murder conviction |\n| Nikolay Soltys | 466 | Aug 23, 2001 | Committed suicide in jail (2002) before trial |\n| Clayton Lee Waagner | 467 | Sep 21, 2001 | Convicted of anthrax hoaxes, firearms, escape, theft—not murder |\n\n## Sources\n- FBI Ten Most Wanted 401–500 list: https://www.fbi.gov/wanted/topten/ten-most-wanted-fugitives-faq/ten-most-wanted-401-500\n- Wikipedia \"FBI Ten Most Wanted Fugitives, 2000s\": https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FBI_Ten_Most_Wanted_Fugitives,_2000s\n- Individual case records from court opinions (FindLaw, Justia, Casemine), FBI press releases, and contemporaneous news coverage (CNN, Orlando Sentinel, Chicago Tribune, Philadelphia Inquirer, LA Times, Jamaica Observer) as cited in the delegation transcripts.",
